.TITLE "uname"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Displays system information. It reports details about the __operating system__, kernel version, and hardware architecture of the local machine.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**uname**
Displays the name of the operating system kernel (Darwin on macOS).
> 

**uname -a**
Displays all available system information in a single line.
> __-a__ all information flag

**uname -m**
Shows the hardware architecture name, such as x86_64 or arm64.
> __-m__ machine architecture flag

**uname -r**
Displays the specific release version of the operating system kernel.
> __-r__ release flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
On macOS, __uname__ identifies the system as Darwin. Checking the hardware architecture with __uname -m__ is particularly useful on modern Macs to determine if the system is running on Intel or Apple Silicon.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:sw_vers** **mac:sysctl**

